#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:1
msgid ""
"ADR-0023: Buses of lanes, implicit packing and explicit injection of "
"telescope arrays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P15.6 (also P15.7, P15.8, P15.9)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:9
#, python-format
msgid ""
"A `ModalField` carried N *channels* on a single port, and its last axis "
"mixed two notions: waveguides separated in space (the outputs of a "
"`TelescopeArray`, the guides of a chip) and the modes of one guide (the "
"`modes` port of a `Fiber`). A `TelescopeArray` returned such a field "
"directly, so collecting the light in free space and injecting it into "
"single-mode guides were one element with an ideal coupling: no coupling "
"loss (an Airy pupil couples at most about 80 % of its power into a "
"single-mode fibre, Shaklan & Roddier 1988, Appl. Opt. 27, 2334), no "
"antenna lobe of the fibre (off-axis sources coupled like on-axis ones, "
"which distorts the transmission maps of nullers), and nothing could be "
"placed on one arm before the injection. The review of 19/10/2026 and its "
"decisions of 20/10 ([pistes d'évolution "
"§1](../specs/pistes_evolution.md)) settle the model; this record fixes "
"its design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:18
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:20
msgid ""
"**A lane is one signal.** A guided lane is a `ModalField` of one guide, "
"of shape `(sources, λ, modes)` (`modes = 1` for a single-mode guide); its"
" mode axis never designates different guides any more. A free-space lane "
"is a `Wavefront`, a `Wavecube` or an `IncoherentBundle`. `ModalField` "
"counts are renamed accordingly: `n_sources` (incoherent inputs, was "
"`n_modes`), `n_modes` (was `n_channels`), `mode_power` (was "
"`channel_power`); `labels` name the modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:25
msgid ""
"**A bus** (`lumos.fields.Bus`) groups N lanes of the same signal class, "
"separated in space (guides of a chip, arms of an interferometer). It "
"behaves as a sequence (`len(bus)`, `bus[i]`, iteration) and carries per-"
"lane metadata: names (`T1`…`Tn` by default) and, when known, the "
"projected position of the telescope that feeds the lane (used by "
"`FizeauCombiner`). Spectral components, incoherent components (sources) "
"and the modes of one guide are never lanes: separating them is the job of"
" a physical component (prism, dichroic, photonic lantern)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:31
msgid ""
"**Implicit packing.** A bus stores its lanes in a single array when they "
"share their metadata, and as a list otherwise; the choice is made when "
"the bus is built (and after every `Mux`), and the interface is the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:34
msgid ""
"guided: same sources, wavelengths, spectral weights, power unit and "
"number of sources; the number of modes may differ between lanes. The "
"array is `(sources, λ, Σ modes)` with the offset of each lane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:36
msgid ""
"free space: same class and identical metadata (grid, sources, "
"wavelengths, weights, polarisation, power unit: the auxiliary data of the"
" signal as a JAX pytree) and the same array shape. The array is `(lanes, "
"*lane_shape)`. `Bus.packing_problem(lanes)` says why lanes cannot be "
"packed; a bus is a JAX pytree in both forms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:40
msgid ""
"**Source lists are identified.** `ModalField` and `IncoherentBundle` "
"carry `sources`, an identifier of the source list they describe (a digest"
" of directions, wavelengths and fluxes, set by `Telescope` and "
"`TelescopeArray`, kept by every element, `None` when unknown). Lanes "
"interfere only if they describe the same sources in the same order, so "
"packing requires equal identifiers and a recombiner (any component whose "
"matrix mixes lanes) refuses lanes that cannot be packed, with the reason,"
" instead of assuming it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:45
msgid ""
"**Ports declare buses.** `Input(..., bus=True)` receives a bus (or a "
"single lane) as it is; `Output(..., bus=True)` produces one. The signal "
"type of a port stays the type of its lanes, so the compatibility of two "
"ports does not change; the flag tells the editor to draw the port as a "
"bus (P15.7) and is published in the JSON schema of the element (`x-lumos-"
"ports[].bus`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:49
msgid ""
"**A one-lane component applied to a bus acts on every lane.** "
"`Element.apply` maps an element over the lanes when a bus reaches an "
"input that does not declare `bus=True`, as N identical copies of the "
"element: every bus input must have the same number of lanes (other inputs"
" are shared), every output becomes a bus with the names and positions of "
"the input bus, and a stochastic element draws an independent stream per "
"lane (its random key gets the lane index), as N copies would. An element "
"with a data output (camera, processing) cannot be mapped: its outputs "
"would not be signals of one lane each; it asks the user to recombine or "
"`Demux` the bus first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:56
msgid "**Elements migrated.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:57
msgid ""
"Photonic components take and return guided buses. `channels` lists "
"**lanes** (all when empty); a diagonal component (waveguide, phase "
"shifter) acts on each selected lane; a mixing component applies its "
"matrix to the vector of all the modes of its selected lanes, writes the "
"outputs back on the same lanes when it has as many outputs as input "
"modes, and otherwise puts single-mode output lanes where its first "
"selected lane was."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:62
msgid ""
"`Fiber` takes one free-space lane; on a bus it is mapped (one fibre per "
"lane) and returns a bus of guided lanes on `modes` and a bus of near "
"fields on `out`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:64
msgid ""
"`Photodiode` and `PowerMeter` read a lane as one value (the power of all "
"its modes or pixels) and a bus as one value per lane (axis `channel`, "
"setting `channel` of the power meter = a lane)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:66
msgid ""
"`TelescopeArray` (P15.6) returns a packed bus of single-mode guided lanes"
" with the positions of its telescopes; P15.8 renames this ideal model "
"`IdealInjectionArray` and makes `TelescopeArray` return a bus of "
"`IncoherentBundle` in the pupil plane (one pupil per telescope, the "
"geometric phase of its arm), the injection becoming an explicit `Fiber`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:70
msgid ""
"**Format `.lumos` 1.3.** Connections are unchanged (a connection carries "
"a whole bus). Version 1.3 records that `channels` designate lanes and, "
"from P15.8, that `TelescopeArray` is the free-space array: reading a "
"1.0–1.2 document converts it (a `TelescopeArray` becomes an "
"`IdealInjectionArray`, which keeps the results identical). Documents in "
"which `channels` addressed the modes of a multimode `Fiber` (no shipped "
"preset did) cannot be converted automatically; the converter logs a "
"warning naming the component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:75
msgid ""
"**`Demux(N)` and `Mux(N)`** (P15.7) are pure elements of the core: "
"`Demux` splits a bus into N one-lane buses (keeping names and positions),"
" `Mux` stacks lanes side by side without mixing them (an unconnected "
"input becomes an empty lane, zero amplitude, with a warning at "
"validation). On packed buses they are slices and concatenations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:80
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:82
msgid ""
"**Lanes addressed in connections** (`\"to\": \"mmi.in[2]\"`, option A of "
"the review): one wire per guide without extra blocks, but connections to "
"a lane, assembly of lanes and their validation in the engine, and a new "
"syntax in the format. B + C gives the same drawing with two pure "
"elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:85
msgid ""
"**Keeping the channel axis and adding a separate mode axis to "
"`ModalField`** (`(sources, λ, lanes, modes)`): every lane would need the "
"same number of modes, which a bus of a multimode fibre and single-mode "
"guides does not have, and free-space signals would still need another "
"mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:88
msgid ""
"**Always a list of lanes**: simpler, but a recombiner would copy the "
"lanes at every component and a fibre per arm could not be vectorised "
"(P15.3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:90
msgid ""
"**Checking the sources by their number only**: two telescopes pointed at "
"different source lists of the same length would interfere silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:93
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:95
msgid ""
"Code and tests that built a multi-channel `ModalField` for a chip now "
"build a bus (`Bus.guided`); the photonic, fibre and detector tests are "
"rewritten accordingly (`test(P15.6)!`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:97
msgid ""
"A power meter or photodiode on the `modes` output of a multimode fibre "
"reads the total guided power instead of one value per mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0023-buses.md:99
msgid ""
"`Demux`, `Mux`, the bus rendering, `IdealInjectionArray`, the free-space "
"`TelescopeArray` and `FizeauCombiner` build on this model (P15.7 to "
"P15.9); P15.3 vectorises mapped elements on packed buses."
msgstr ""

